      <abstract>The New England Congregational Church in Manhattan, New York, N.Y., was gathered in
        1866. A building for the church was constructed near the corner of Forty-First Street. The
        church dissolved in 1872 with its membership largely moving to help form the Madison Avenue
        Congregational Church. This collection contains both administrative and membership-related
        materials and includes church records and meeting minutes, registers, and other membership
        materials.</abstract>
